events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Since swizzling is only really useful from bindings (nobody will call `swizzled_set` by hand), I think it should entirely live in the core binds instead of core.\r\n\r\nI haven't looked at the rest of the PR yet.\r\n\r\nEdit: As to Holon's comment; agreed. The problem is the many configurations of `template <typename V, int comp1, int comp2, int comp3, int comp4>`, leading to a template explosion.\r\nSwizzling should be solved without templates, resolving indices at runtime (if we do decide to add it, which I'm not sure there is a consensus on?).","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118203#pullrequestreview-4059240078","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118203","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118203#pullrequestreview-4059240078"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118203"}},"submitted_at":"2026-04-05T07:52:04Z","commit_id":null}]